#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""glaeda-cmux-runner: turn a cmux Mac mini into a GitHub Actions self-hosted runner.

    glaeda-cmux-runner                                plan: what --apply would do (no side effects)
    glaeda-cmux-runner --apply                        download, verify, register, load the LaunchAgent
    glaeda-cmux-runner --uninstall                    plan removal
    glaeda-cmux-runner --uninstall --apply            deregister and remove what --apply installed
    glaeda-mini-setup --runner [...]                  same thing, through the mini setup front door

Defaults register to --repo manaflow-ai/cmux. Use --org ORG for an organization runner.
A fleet member passes --manifest M --member NAME instead of --labels: its class, availability and
verified Xcodes become the labels, and a later change re-registers it in place (docs/CMUX_MINI_RUNNER.md 2c).

What --apply does, all under $HOME and owned by the current user (no sudo):
    1. picks an official actions/runner osx-arm64 release: --runner-version, else the version another
       instance on this mini runs, else one already cached here, else the latest the fleet operator resolved,
       else the API (once; authenticated when it can be), else a pinned fallback (resolve_release). It
       verifies the tarball's SHA-256 (release notes, asset digest, or pin), keeps it in a per-mini cache
       (~/Library/Caches/glaeda/actions-runner/<version>, with a release.json marker) so the mini downloads
       a version once, and unpacks it into ~/actions-runner-glaeda (or --runner-dir)
    2. registers it with labels self-hosted,macOS,ARM64,glaeda-mini (+ --labels), persistent
       (not ephemeral) so the _work tree keeps hot state between jobs
    3. writes job hooks: job-started refuses fork pull requests and pull_request_target and
       runs glaeda-disk pressure; job-completed runs disk pressure again (never fatal)
    4. writes and loads ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.teamleaderleo.glaeda.cmux-runner.plist
    5. confirms the registration through the GitHub API

Headless fleet members can pass --headless. That explicit mode installs a
system LaunchDaemon as the current user through passwordless sudo, with
UserName set to the runner account. It is intended for EC2 Macs where a
per-user LaunchAgent has no GUI domain.

The one-time registration token comes from `gh api -X POST .../registration-token` on stdout.
It is never placed in any argv, written to disk, or printed. It reaches config.sh only through
ACTIONS_RUNNER_INPUT_TOKEN in that one child's environment, which the runner reads and clears.

A mini without gh (or without admin credentials on it) takes the token on stdin instead, minted
on the operator's own machine, so no GitHub credential ever lands on the mini:

    gh api -X POST repos/OWNER/REPO/actions/runners/registration-token --jq .token \
      | ssh MINI glaeda-cmux-runner --apply --repo OWNER/REPO --token-stdin

Without gh the release, when step 1 needs the API at all, is read with curl (with GH_TOKEN or
GITHUB_TOKEN from the environment when set, sent on curl's stdin), a name collision is left to
config.sh (which refuses one), and step 5 is confirmed locally from the runner log instead.

Routing is never automated. A --labels runner's plan prints the `gh variable set` commands that
point cmux workflows at the glaeda-mini label, and the `gh variable delete` commands that roll back.
A fleet member (--manifest, or a receipt that recorded one) prints no MACOS_RUNNER_* line: cmux's PR
pool picker already routes to its pool labels, and those variables would bypass the picker. A trusted
member prints the nightly variables (CI_SEED_TRUSTED_POOL, CI_NIGHTLY_TRUSTED_RUNNER) instead.
The receipt lands in ~/.local/state/glaeda/cmux-runner/receipt.json.

Stale copies and label drift. On a host with an over-the-air release installed (glaeda-update), a copy
of this script whose runner files differ from that release's and are older than it (by its
.glaeda-source.json stamp, its release, or its git commit date; unknown counts as older) blocks: the
plan says which copy to run instead, and the release's plan labels are compared with this copy's.
--allow-stale overrides. The register step lists every label drift it sees: the receipt's or GitHub's
registered labels against what this version would register.

    glaeda-cmux-runner --refresh-hooks [--apply]      plan, then install, this copy's hook files only

--refresh-hooks brings the two files every runner install copies unchanged into its glaeda-hooks/
(glaeda-cmux-runner-hook and glaeda_reservation.py) to this copy's bytes, in each runner directory a
receipt under ~/.local/state/glaeda/cmux-runner owns. It is how glaeda-update rolls a hook fix out
(docs/GLAEDA_OTA.md), and runs only from a release's copy: it replaces a file only when its bytes are a
version the release descends from (hook-history.json), so it never downgrades. It writes each file
atomically with the mode --apply gives it and touches nothing else: no registration, labels, generated
wrappers, LaunchAgent or receipt. A runner with a job running is left for the next run; a runner whose
wrappers call the hook with arguments the staged new hook rejects (--parse-only, from glaeda-hooks/, with
the wrapper's own interpreter) is refused, since a rejected job-started fails jobs. It shares one lock
with --apply and --uninstall. The running listener gate re-execs the new hook itself (Gate.reload) and
keeps its runner.
"""

